    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nTucked away in a quiet laneway beneath the shadow of St. Canice's Cathedral, 5 Loreto View is one of those rare properties that quietly defies expectation.\n\nFrom the street, this charming cottage reveals little of what lies beyond its front door. Its modest faade sits comfortably amongst the historic character of Irishtown, blending seamlessly into one of Kilkenny's most evocative and atmospheric quarters. Yet step inside and an entirely different world unfolds.\n\nLike a carefully guarded secret in the very heart of the city, the house opens into a surprisingly spacious and beautifully designed home extending to approximately 127.3 sq.m. Every room has been thoughtfully planned and meticulously finished, creating a home that is both elegant and effortlessly comfortable.\n\nThe journey through the property is a delightful one. The welcoming front living room, centred around a handsome fireplace and lined with bookshelves, offers the perfect place to retreat with a book on a winter's evening. Beyond, the house gradually reveals its greatest surprise.\n\nTo the rear lies a magnificent open-plan kitchen, dining and living space, flooded with natural light from a soaring vaulted ceiling and an impressive wall of glass that frames the garden beyond. It is a room designed for gathering, entertaining and everyday living. Throughout the day, sunlight pours into the space while the changing colours of the garden become a living backdrop to the home.\n\nThe connection between house and garden is particularly special. Large double glazed doors blur the line between indoors and outdoors, drawing the eye towards a beautifully sheltered private garden that seems entirely removed from the bustle of city life. Mature planting, colourful borders, lawn and patio combine to create a wonderfully tranquil setting. It is difficult to believe that Kilkenny's vibrant city centre lies only moments away.\n\nIndeed, seclusion is perhaps the home's most remarkable quality. Situated just a short stroll from cafs, restaurants, boutiques and the cultural attractions that make Kilkenny one of Ireland's most celebrated cities, the property enjoys an almost unique sense of privacy. It is a genuine oasis, hidden in plain sight.\n\nAccommodation comprises a generous living room, two bedrooms, two bathrooms, utility room and the stunning open-plan kitchen, dining and living area. The spacious first-floor landing offers additional flexibility, making it ideal as a study, reading area or occasional workspace.\n\nThe location requires little introduction. Nestled behind the magnificent St. Canice's Cathedral and Round Tower, Loreto View forms part of the historic fabric of medieval Kilkenny. Cobbled streets, ancient stone walls and centuries of history surround the property, yet every modern convenience is within easy walking distance.\n\nOpportunities to acquire a home of such character, privacy and charm in the centre of Kilkenny are exceptionally rare. 5 Loreto View is more than a house. It is a hidden retreat, a peaceful sanctuary and a beautifully crafted home in one of Ireland's most enchanting urban settings.\n\nA secret garden in the heart of the city. A hidden sanctuary beneath the cathedral. A home that reveals its magic only to those fortunate enough to step inside.\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n"
      },
